	// ModParser.lua:690-703, the ten `minimum`/`maximum <type> damage` rows interleaved with the
	// five above. ⚠️ THEIR ABSENCE DID NOT DROP A MOD, IT BUILT A WRONG ONE AND THEN DROPPED THE
	// LINE: "50% less Minimum Lightning Damage" matched the plain `lightning damage` row, produced
	// `LightningDamage MORE -50` — a mod against ALL lightning damage, not its minimum — and left
	// " Minimum " as the unmatched remainder, which discards the whole line. Both halves of the
	// Lightning Mastery pair went that way, so ours ran min HIGH by exactly 2.00 and max LOW by
	// exactly 0.80 on the same builds. The consumers (CalcOffence.lua:116-119) were already ported
	// at calc_offence.go:182-185, so this was a correct consumer with no producer.
	//
	// ⚠️ THE PHYSICAL PAIR IS ALREADY HERE AND A GREP FOR IT MISSES: it sits in the alphabetical
	// block above (`minimum physical damage` / `maximum physical damage`, lines 345 and 349) spelt
	// with BACKTICKS, so a search for the quoted form reports all ten as absent. That is why this
	// block is the EIGHT elemental and chaos rows rather than PoB's full ten.
	"minimum lightning damage": {names: []string{"MinLightningDamage"}},
	"maximum lightning damage": {names: []string{"MaxLightningDamage"}},
