	// ModParser.lua:2763-2766. ⚠️ THIS WAS AN INVENTED IMPLEMENTATION. The pin emits TWO minion
	// modifiers -- the Elemancer flag and `ElementalDamageTaken MORE -100`. We emitted SIX:
	// Fire/Cold/LightningResist and their three *ResistMax siblings, each OVERRIDE 100.
	//
	// That reaches a similar outcome in the GAME's terms and a completely different one in the
	// GRADED terms: every elemental resistance stat on a golem minion read 100 where PoB reads
	// the creature's own base (40 / 70 / 75). `task overapplied-census` put Minion.ColdResist and
	// Minion.LightningResist at EXACTLY 2.5x on 119 builds each, and stat-ratios concentrated 70
	// of those into one exact-2.5000 cluster dominated by golem builds.
	//
	// ⚠️ ONLY 1 CORPUS BUILD CARRIES THIS AS ITEM TEXT -- the rest get it from the Elementalist's
	// Liege of the Primordial ascendancy, so `corpus-grep` says 1 of 3771. Tree-sourced mods
	// invert the usual grep bound; size this from the STAT, never from the grep.
	//
	// ⚠️ `Elemancer` HAS NO CONSUMER IN THIS TREE and is ported anyway, deliberately. It is the
	// pin's flag, and inventing a substitute for a name we do not consume is precisely what
	// produced the six overrides above. The MORE mod does have one: calc_defence.go:1684.
	"summoned golems are immune to elemental damage": []mod.Mod{
		MOD("MinionModifier", "LIST", mod.MinionModifier{Mod: FLAG("Elemancer")}).Tag(mod.SkillType(string(data.SkillTypeGolem))),
		MOD("MinionModifier", "LIST", mod.MinionModifier{Mod: MOD("ElementalDamageTaken", "MORE", -100)}).Tag(mod.SkillType(string(data.SkillTypeGolem))),
	},
