	// ModParser.lua:3484-3487 -- the ENEMY's own damage conversion. ⚠️ THIS FAMILY AND ITS ONLY
	// CONSUMER (CalcDefence.lua:1721-1777) WERE BOTH ABSENT, which is the one arrangement where
	// either half alone measures exactly zero: a mod nothing reads and a block nothing feeds are
	// each indistinguishable from a wrong theory. They land together on purpose.
	//
	// The largest arm is Shaper of Flames (tree node 53123, Elementalist) at 40%; the 10/20/25%
	// arms reach the same three ailment rows from other sources, which is why the rows are
	// parameterised over the damage types rather than written out per percentage.
	`nearby enemies convert (\d+)% of their ([a-z]+) damage to ([a-z]+)`:                     enemyDamageConvertRow(""),
	`enemies ignited by you have (\d+)% of ([a-z]+) damage they deal converted to ([a-z]+)`:  enemyDamageConvertRow("Ignited"),
	`enemies shocked by you have (\d+)% of ([a-z]+) damage they deal converted to ([a-z]+)`:  enemyDamageConvertRow("Shocked"),
	`enemies poisoned by you have (\d+)% of ([a-z]+) damage they deal converted to ([a-z]+)`: enemyDamageConvertRow("Poisoned"),
