	// Minions
	// Upstream is ONE name carrying a BASE PERCENTAGE, not two flags. The flag encoding was
	// lossy in a way a name-set check cannot see: both spellings produce the mod name the
	// consumer reads, and only the TYPE says whether it gets 100, 50 or a bare true.
	//
	// ⚠️ IT ALSO COLLAPSED TWO SOURCES INTO ONE. Two items each granting the full form summed to
	// 100 under the flag and sum to 200 here, which is what upstream does.
	//
	// The consumer (calc_perform.go, CalcPerform.lua:1207-1209) reads the BASE form first and
	// falls back to the two flags only when it is 0, so it was correct before this change and is
	// correct after. Its flag arms are now unreachable; retiring them is a change to a file this
	// branch does not own and is routed rather than made here.
	//pob:src/Modules/ModParser.lua:4372
	"your strength is added to your minions": []mod.Mod{MOD("StrengthAddedToMinions", "BASE", float64(100))},
	//pob:src/Modules/ModParser.lua:4373
	"half of your strength is added to your minions": []mod.Mod{MOD("StrengthAddedToMinions", "BASE", float64(50))},
