	// commit: e9d30e392, "Fix ailment immune applying 100% ailment avoid (#6297)". The comment
	// and the test that pinned the old behaviour outlived the condition they described --
	// exactly a known bad shape, and they read as considered for that whole time.
	//
	// ⚠️ AND THE SAME UPSTREAM COMMIT MOVED THIS WHOLE FAMILY OFF Avoid<Ailment> BASE 100 AND
	// ONTO flag("<Ailment>Immune"), which is the audit's "40 of 130 rows" row. That conversion
	// is NOT made here and must not be: of the six flags the pin now uses, only ShockImmune and
	// ChillImmune have a reader in this tree (calc_perform.go) and FreezeImmune, IgniteImmune,
	// BleedImmune and PoisonImmune have none at all, while every Avoid<Ailment> name being
	// replaced does have readers (calc_defence.go, configs.go, calc_perform.go). Converting the
	// parser half alone would delete working behaviour rather than port anything.
	//
	// RETIRING CONDITION: re-check when calc_defence.go/calc_perform.go grow readers for all
	// six Immune flags; the conversion is a single family and belongs in that same change.
